From 849a463b666df2fa923533f0af81c636639c14f5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matt Levine <blahm1d@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 4 Jul 2026 14:52:34 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 10/12] core: P0014 - implement MOVE @SAddr,@DAddr (mem-to-mem
 absolute field move)

The TMS34010 MOVE @SAddr,@DAddr (0x05C0/0x0DC0, both operands absolute
32-bit addresses, 5-word encoding) was never decoded -- birdybro had the
register-indirect M2M and single-address abs load/store, but not abs-to-abs.

Wiring real inputs (Phase 4) put the game on its true attract path, where
the display-interrupt handler uses it for per-frame palette work
(MOVE @1086210h,@18103D0h at ffe0e480, mainram->palette). With inputs
stubbed to 0 the boot ran clean; with real inputs it hit 0x05C0 as an
illegal opcode.

Fix: new iclass INSTR_MOVE_ABS_M2M + CORE_FETCH_IMM2_LO/HI states + a
second immediate (imm2_lo/hi -> imm2_32 = DAddr); a two-step CORE_MEMORY
transaction (step 0 reads the mv_fs field at imm32=SAddr into move_data_q,
step 1 writes it to imm2_32=DAddr), modelled on INSTR_MOVE_FIELD_M2M.
Post-fix the boot runs the main loop with no illegal opcode. MM TBs pass.

